From 26d05e92abacd8c6791917cb2b2a80eedcd32550 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MedSphere Agent <agent@medsphere.local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:06:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: V1 centralized monitoring and alerting foundation

- add packages/common/src/metrics/metrics-registry.ts: dependency-free
  Counter/Histogram primitives with a hard label-key allowlist
  (service/method/route/status_class/dependency/outcome/channel/
  provider only -- rejects any other key, including tenantId/phone/
  requestId, at record time), a cardinality cap, Prometheus text
  exposition, and an OTLP-metrics-model-shaped JSON snapshot; exported
  as a singleton (appMetrics) to avoid changing constructor signatures
  on already-accepted, already-tested classes
- add packages/common/src/metrics/otlp-exporter.ts: bounded, fail-safe
  OTLP/HTTP+JSON push exporter -- disabled by default, fails closed on
  malformed config (non-HTTPS endpoint, out-of-bounds timeout, missing
  named credential-reference variable), never throws on backend
  outage, rate-limits its own failure logging (every 10th consecutive
  failure) to prevent log storms
- add GET /metrics (Prometheus text exposition) via new
  MetricsController/MetricsModule, matching HealthController's public-
  endpoint convention
- wire HTTP request count/duration/status-class metrics into the
  existing request-observability middleware (reusing its safeMethod/
  safeRouteTemplate helpers, not duplicating them)
- wire a bounded server-error metric into GlobalExceptionFilter (adds
  an optional, backward-compatible serviceName constructor parameter)
- wire dependency readiness metrics (count + duration, by
  postgresql/redis) into AuthReadinessService, preserving its existing
  sequential short-circuit behavior exactly
- wire notification-delivery metrics (channel + outcome only --
  tenantId/deliveryId/errorCode deliberately excluded from labels)
  into the existing LoggingNotificationDeliveryObserver
- wire OTP dispatch and reservation-outcome metrics at their existing
  call sites via transparent, non-behavior-altering wrappers
- start the OTLP exporter from main.ts only when explicitly enabled;
  a malformed export config disables export only (logged once) and
  never prevents the service from starting
- add packages/common test infra (had none before) matching
  packages/logger's established build-then-node:test convention;
  25 new tests, all passing for real against the compiled build
- re-ran all pre-existing request-observability, error-observability
  tests: all still pass unchanged (8/8)
- extend docs/operations/v1-observability-runbook.md: architecture,
  metrics catalog, exporter configuration, SLO definitions (explicitly
  labeled initial engineering thresholds, not a contractual SLA),
  alert-rule summary, expanded dashboard specification, expanded
  incident workflow, and an explicit 'what still requires production
  deployment/vendor activation' section
- add docs/operations/v1-alert-rules.prometheus.yml: 12 real,
  executable, provider-neutral Prometheus alerting rules across 4
  groups (availability, HTTP, workflows, telemetry), each with a
  bounded evaluation window and warning/critical severity -- validated
  as parseable YAML with the expected rule structure
- add .env.example placeholders only for the new TELEMETRY_* variables
  and an example credential-reference variable; no real credentials
- does not add any OpenTelemetry SDK dependency, any paid monitoring
  service, or require any real vendor account
- does not touch 0004/0005/0006 (parked patches) -- confirmed absent
  from this branch
